---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Learning English from Friends</h1>
			<div class="intro">
				<p>
					Hey, I'm Qi. I've lived abroad for many years, but I still
					learn something new in English every day.
				</p>
				<p>
					Since moving to the Netherlands last year, I've come across
					even more words, expressions, and little language
					differences that I had never noticed before.
				</p>
				<p>
					This blog is my personal English-learning journal: a place
					to write down the words, expressions, mistakes, and small
					discoveries I pick up from everyday life.
				</p>
				<p>
					The idea was inspired by Carnegie Mellon University
					Associate Teaching Professor Terry E. Lee's <cite
						>Learning English from Friends</cite
					>. He taught me Data Structures for Application Programmers
					at CMU and was a wonderful professor. I loved his idea of
					learning English not only from textbooks, but also from
					conversations, daily experiences, and the people around us.
				</p>
				<p>
					Here, I keep track of the little things I learn along the
					way.
				</p>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.intro {
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}
</style>
